{"body":"S03 is the portable authorization/parser milestone in the canonical [task graph](https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/blob/main/docs/restart/work-items.json). This issue is navigation, not a second status ledger.\n\nAuthor: `/root/s03_author`, isolated branch `restart/s03-authorization`. Inputs: nsealr `3cbd818a0bcd4016eb8983dad7605cb57280d913`, accepted P01 requirements and integrated S02 secret ownership.\n\nFirst deliver an exact source-backed specification and acceptance plan for one canonical reviewed operation, one-use authority, invalidation/race behavior, strict bounded parsing, honest Unicode presentation and independent vectors. Product changes await specification approval and distinct final review. Physical input/display qualification and complete signing remain their declared device/K01 gates; no host approval flag substitutes for them.\n\nAcceptance is unchanged in the graph. Record exact candidates, red/positive/negative checks and source-bound independent review before integration.\n","number":17,"state":"OPEN","title":"S03: bind local review to one canonical operation and one execution","url":"https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/issues/17"}
